    "result_text": "The full suite passed \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class (the other two files are a base class and a support helper), and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec asked that an owner's `timezone` be derived from its locality/region via the fixed table NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney, VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne, QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane. I made three coordinated changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `timezone` read-only string field to the owner response schema (right after `locality`), documenting the region-to-timezone table. This drives the generated `OwnerDto`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `REGION_TIMEZONE` lookup map and a `@Transient getTimezone()` derived getter that maps `getLocality()` through the table, returning `null` for any other region (consistent with how the other derived getters behave).\n\n3. The existing MapStruct `OwnerMapper` auto-maps the same-named `timezone` property from `Owner` to `OwnerDto`, so no mapper change was needed.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion`) creates a Sydney owner (postcode 2000 \u2192 NSW) and asserts `$.locality == \"NSW\"` and `$.timezone == \"Australia/Sydney\"` \u2014 it now passes, and the build reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
