    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits the existing structure of `Owner` naturally. The entity already carries derived, `@Transient` accessors (`getLocality()`, the `customerCode`/dash parsing, `getIdentityKey()`), so adding `getTimezone()` as another derived getter alongside them is consistent with the established idiom rather than introducing a new pattern.\n\n- The fixed lookup is correctly expressed as a `private static final Map` constant via `Map.of(...)`, colocated with the getter that uses it \u2014 the right unit for a region\u2192timezone mapping that belongs to the owner's locality.\n- `getTimezone()` delegates to the existing `getLocality()` rather than re-deriving the region, so there's no duplication of the locality-extraction logic.\n- The OpenAPI `timezone` property is added adjacent to the related `locality`/region field, with documentation mirroring the Javadoc, which is where a maintainer would expect it.\n- Nothing here turns `Owner` into a catch-all beyond what it already is (a model with several derived accessors); this is a small, coherent addition.",
